prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a 3D car showroom. Load two car models (ToyCar.glb and ToyCar.glb), display them on exhibition platforms, and support selection, color adjustment, and automatic rotation.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/ToyCar.glb and assets/ToyCar.glb separately;
(2) After loading, scale both cars to appropriate sizes and place them on the two exhibition platforms respectively;
(3) After all models have finished loading, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[Showroom Layout]
(4) Create the showroom floor (PlaneGeometry, dark gray 0x333333, size 20x20);
(5) Create two exhibition platforms (CylinderGeometry, white 0xeeeeee, radius 2, height 0.3), positioned at (-4, 0.15, 0) and (4, 0.15, 0);
(6) Place the Ferrari on the left exhibition platform and the ToyCar on the right exhibition platform;
(7) Initially position the camera at (0, 5, 10) and use OrbitControls;

[Selection Interaction]
(8) Use a Raycaster to detect mouse clicks on the vehicles. After a vehicle is clicked:
  a) The selected car receives a spotlight shining from above (SpotLight, white, relatively high intensity);
  b) Turn off or reduce the intensity of the spotlight on the unselected car;
  c) Update __3D_STATE__.selectedCar to "ferrari" or "toycar";
(9) Clicking an empty area cancels the selection and sets selectedCar to "none";

[Color Adjustment]
(10) The UI panel on the right displays the name of the currently selected vehicle (id="carName");
(11) Provide a hue slider (id="hueSlider", type=range, min=0, max=360) that adjusts the overall hue of the selected vehicle;
(12) Implement color changing by traversing all MeshStandardMaterial instances in the vehicle model and modifying the H value of each material color's HSL;

[Automatic Rotation]
(13) Provide an "Auto Rotate" toggle button (id="autoRotateBtn"). After it is clicked, the selected vehicle rotates uniformly around the Y axis on its exhibition platform at 45 degrees per second;
(14) Clicking it again stops the rotation;

[Environment Lighting]
(15) AmbientLight (intensity 0.4) + DirectionalLight (intensity 0.8);
(16) The showroom has a subtle environmental reflection effect;

[HUD Display]
(17) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Selected vehicle (id="selectedDisplay")
  - Current hue value (id="hueValue")
  - Rotation status (id="rotateStatus")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean (whether both cars have finished loading)
  - selectedCar: string ("ferrari" / "toycar" / "none")
  - hueValue: number (current hue, 0-360)
  - autoRotate: boolean (whether automatic rotation is enabled)
  - ferrariPosition: { x: number, y: number, z: number } (Ferrari position)
  - toycarPosition: { x: number, y: number, z: number } (ToyCar position)
  - cameraDistance: number (distance from the camera to the origin)

Output a single HTML file. Place this file in the same directory as the assets/ folder and run it through a local HTTP server.
